# TieTrace public demo behind Caddy on a bare IP, no domain. See DEPLOY.md section 9. Aaryan, Oct 18 2026.
#
# WARNING: this is plain HTTP. The basic-auth password AND every visitor's API key cross the internet
# unencrypted, so anyone on the path can read them. Prefer the SSH tunnel (DEPLOY.md section 11), or get a
# domain and use deploy/Caddyfile. Use this only for a short demo with throwaway keys.
#
# A template: DEPLOY.md fills USER_HERE and HASH_HERE (bcrypt, from `caddy hash-password`) with sed and writes the
# result to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (root:caddy, mode 640). Caddy flushes text/event-stream (SSE) at once by itself.

http://:80 {
	basic_auth {
		USER_HERE HASH_HERE
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
